Thanks for working on this - I took over and pushed a slightly different design on top:
* the reason now lives in `Cancellation` and gets forwarded to delegated executions (`MultiAgent`, `SpeechAgent`, `TraceableAgent`)
* `getResult()` throws a new `CancellationException` with `hasReason()`/`getReason()` - the message stays the same, so the reason isn't baked into the exception text
* dropped the `UPGRADE.md` entry, since `ExecutionInterface` isn't released yet => no BC break
